  "words": "For thousands of years, a chain of volcanic islands sat completely isolated off the eastern coast of Asia, cut off from the rest of the world by violent oceans and stormy seas. On these mist-covered mountains, a culture developed that was unlike anything else on Earth. It was a place where gentle poets wrote verses about falling cherry blossoms, while brutal warlords chopped off heads with razor-sharp steel. It was a nation that completely locked its doors to the outside world for two and a half centuries,"
